      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We start by recognizing that the numerator, $235^2 - 221^2$, is a difference of squares. The difference of squares formula states that $a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)$. Applying this formula, we have:\n\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = (235 - 221)(235 + 221)\n\\]\n\nCalculating the values inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n235 - 221 = 14\n\\]\n\\[\n235 + 221 = 456\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = 14 \\times 456\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to compute $14 \\times 456$. We can do this by breaking it down into smaller multiplications:\n\n\\[\n14 \\times 456 = 14 \\times (400 + 50 + 6) = 14 \\times 400 + 14 \\times 50 + 14 \\times 6\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n\\[\n14 \\times 400 = 5600\n\\]\n\\[\n14 \\times 50 = 700\n\\]\n\\[\n14 \\times 6 = 84\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n5600 + 700 + 84 = 6384\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = 6384\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the value of $\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}$. Substituting the value we found:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14} = \\frac{6384}{14}\n\\]\n\nPerforming the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14} = 456\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{456}\n\\]",
